"comparison": "Both Microsoft and Bank of America establish formal processes to monitor risk levels and escalate significant issues to management-level committees or the Board. Microsoft specifies that 'significant cybersecurity risks are escalated from these [management-level cybersecurity risk] committees to our Non-Financial Risk Committee' (ms_2024_7_P399_S003), whereas Bank of America describes a broader monitoring framework where 'risk limits are breached and have processes to appropriately report and escalate exceptions' to 'managers and alerts to executive management, management-level committees or the Board' (bac_2024_7_P170_S004, bac_2024_7_P170_S005). Both entities utilize management-level committees as a key node for risk escalation, though BAC's disclosure emphasizes the trigger (breach of limits/appetite) while MS emphasizes the specific cybersecurity risk pathway.",
