"comparison": "Both Microsoft and Goldman Sachs disclose the existence of dedicated management-level committees or steering groups specifically tasked with overseeing cybersecurity risk management strategies and frameworks. Microsoft states that 'dedicated management-level cybersecurity risk committees' monitor risks (ms_2024_7_P399_S001). Goldman Sachs mirrors this by stating it has 'a series of committees and steering groups that oversee the implementation of our cybersecurity risk management strategy and framework' (gs_2024_7_P499_S001). Both firms utilize these internal committees to facilitate the reporting of the cybersecurity program's status and incident prevention efforts to senior management.",
